Translation patch: libsignal_protocol::storage::traits (the seven store traits)

Change: under the `extraction` feature, `IdentityKeyStore`, `PreKeyStore`, `SignedPreKeyStore`, `KyberPreKeyStore`, `SessionStore`, `SenderKeyStore` and `ProtocolStore` are left out.
Why: Charon's hax frontend panics on the `#[async_trait]` store traits when `--start-from-pub` roots them, so the extraction leaves out the store-using layer. The protocol and crypto core does not use it.
Behaviour: unchanged in the production build, which does not enable the `extraction` feature.

diff --git a/rust/protocol/src/storage/traits.rs b/rust/protocol/src/storage/traits.rs
